# A separate project. These build an Obsidian "DNA Brain" vault at a hardcoded
# OC2 path and were once intended for the AI GM side, not this framework. They
# import nothing from src/ and nothing here imports them.
build_brain_vault.py
expand_brain_vault.py
# A UTF-16 dump of the 49 wikilinks found in that vault, and the audit report on
# them. The report's twenty "unbuilt" endpoints are all already implemented here
# — it was auditing that vault's page coverage, not this codebase.
unique_links.txt
docs/vault_integrity_report.md

# Graphify's knowledge graph of this repo. Regenerated from the source by
# `graphify extract . --code-only` (local AST, no API calls), so it is derived
# output rather than source: 5.8 MB of it, dominated by graph.html and
# graph.json, both rewritten wholesale on every run.
#
# Graphify's own docs suggest committing this so a team shares one map. Not done
# here because the repo is public and the graph would add megabytes of churn to
# every commit that touches code. Anyone cloning can rebuild it in seconds.
graphify-out/
graph.json

# The working world registry. This is a live world in progress, not source: it
# grows on every run and carries the full prose of every page the decoders
# wrote — 304 KB of it by the time this was untracked. The repository is public
# and the world's own vault is private, so the registry was the one place the
# whole thing was going out.
#
# The repo still ships example data, because a populated registry is the most
# useful thing a stranger can find when trying to get the pipeline running.
# That is data/showcase_registry.json: a curated slice, regenerated by
# scripts/export_showcase.py from data/showcase_names.txt. Edit the names file,
# re-run the script, commit the slice.
#
# Untracking does not unpublish — earlier commits still hold it.
data/world_builder_registry.json

# Pathfinder 2E rules content. Paizo's, not ours, and carried verbatim —
# conditions.json holds their prose word for word, extracted from a third-party
# Obsidian compendium that was itself redistributing it.
#
# Which licence covers it is genuinely unsettled: the corpus mixes pre-Remaster
# terminology (Flat-Footed, an alignment reference) with Remaster terminology
# (ancestry, Holy, Unholy, Void), and those fall under OGL 1.0a and the ORC
# License respectively, which require different notices. Nothing in the files
# records which Paizo works they came from, so a correct attribution notice
# cannot be written from what is here.
#
# The cartridge is a test fixture proving the rules layer hot-swaps between a
# trivial system, a rules-light one and a detailed one. Nothing requires the
# detailed one to be Pathfinder, and nothing requires the data to be published.
# Untracking it removes the redistribution question without touching the
# architecture: resolvers/ is original code, and the full suite passes with
# data/ absent (verified, 1026 tests).
#
# Keep a local copy to exercise the data-backed paths; see LICENSE-NOTICE.md.
src/layer4_rules/PF2EDNA/data/

# Event Ledger databases — runtime state, recreated on demand. Deliberately
# not *.db: the PF2E rules data under src/layer4_rules/PF2EDNA/data/ is
# legitimately tracked and must stay so.
dna_ledger.db
dna_ledger_test.db
*_ledger.db
# sqlite sidecars, should the ledger ever run in WAL mode
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-journal

# Obsidian config (this repo is code; the world bible lives in its own vault)
.obsidian/

# Stray artifacts
Untitled.md
# Created by a script that wrote to a literal path string instead of a real
# path. The real directory name contains fullwidth colon/backslash characters,
# so it is matched by suffix rather than spelled out.
*Hermes/
